---
import '../styles/prose.css';

import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { getApp } from '../data/apps';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const app = getApp('convertit-pro')!;
const appPath = `/apps/${app.slug}/`;

const lastUpdated = new Date('2026-11-04T15:32:39Z');
const lastUpdatedDisplay = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-GB', {
  day: 'numeric',
  month: 'long',
  year: 'numeric',
  hour: '2-digit',
  minute: '2-digit',
  timeZone: 'UTC',
  timeZoneName: 'short',
}).format(lastUpdated);

const title = `${app.name} terms of service`;
const description =
  'Terms of service for Convertit Pro by The Byte Array Ltd: a one-time Google Play purchase, your licence, your files stay on your device, refunds, and your statutory rights.';
---

<Base
  title={title}
  description={description}
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Apps', path: '/apps/' },
    { name: app.name, path: appPath },
    { name: 'Terms of service', path: Astro.url.pathname },
  ]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl pt-4 sm:pt-10" data-pagefind-body>
    <Breadcrumbs
      items={[
        { label: 'Apps', href: '/apps/' },
        { label: app.name, href: appPath },
        { label: 'Terms of service' },
      ]}
    />

    <header class="mt-6 sm:mt-8">
      <h1
        class="font-display text-[clamp(2rem,7.5vw,3.75rem)] leading-[1.04] font-extrabold tracking-[-0.03em] text-balance"
      >
        {title}
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-label-lg text-on-surface-variant">
        Last updated <time datetime={lastUpdated.toISOString()}>{lastUpdatedDisplay}</time>
      </p>
    </header>

    <article class="prose mt-10 sm:mt-12">
      <section>
        <h2>Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          Convertit Pro (“the App”) is published by {site.company.name}, a company registered in{' '}
          {site.company.jurisdiction} (company number{' '}
          <a href={site.company.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-link">{site.company.number}</a>),
          with its registered office at {site.company.office}. In these terms, “we” and “us” mean{' '}
          {site.company.name}, and “you” means the person using the App.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>These terms</h2>
        <p>
          These terms govern your use of the App. By buying, installing or using it, you agree to them. If
          you do not agree, do not use the App. They sit alongside our{' '}
          <a href={app.privacyPath} class="text-link">privacy policy</a> and our{' '}
          <a href="/refund-policy/" class="text-link">refund policy</a>, which are part of your agreement
          with us. Our <a href="/terms/" class="text-link">site terms</a> cover this website. Where the two
          differ, these terms apply to the App.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What the App does</h2>
        <p>
          Convertit Pro is an offline audio, video and image toolkit for Android. It converts media,
          compresses video, reduces noise and includes related tools, and everything runs on your device.
          The current features are listed under What it does on the{' '}
          <a href={appPath} class="text-link">Convertit Pro page</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Price and what your purchase covers</h2>
        <p>
          Convertit Pro is a one-time purchase through Google Play. Google handles the payment and any VAT,
          and we never see your payment details. There are no subscriptions and no in-app charges beyond the
          listed purchase.
        </p>
        <p>
          Your purchase unlocks the tools listed on the Convertit Pro page as of 20 October 2026. We may add
          new tools later. Any that are separate will be listed there before any charge, so a future tool is
          never billed without notice.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Refunds</h2>
        <p>
          Because Google Play handles payment, refunds follow{' '}
          <a
            href="https://support.google.com/googleplay/answer/2479637"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            class="text-link"
          >Google Play’s refund policy</a>. On top of that, our own{' '}
          <a href="/refund-policy/" class="text-link">refund policy</a> gives you a direct route if a feature
          we advertise does not work and we cannot fix it within the time stated there. Nothing here removes
          any refund right you have by law.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Your licence</h2>
        <p>
          Your purchase gives you a personal, non-transferable, non-exclusive licence to install and use the
          App on devices you control, for your own use. You may not sell, rent, sub-license or redistribute
          the App, or copy it except as normal use and the law allow.
        </p>
        <p>
          You may not reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble the App, except where applicable law
          expressly permits it (for example, to achieve interoperability). The App may include open-source
          components that are licensed to you under their own licences. Nothing in these terms limits or
          overrides your rights under those licences.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Your files</h2>
        <p>
          You keep ownership of the files you open and the files the App produces. The App processes your
          files on your device and does not upload them to us or to anyone else. You are responsible for
          keeping your own backups and for having the right to use the files you process. See our{' '}
          <a href={app.privacyPath} class="text-link">privacy policy</a> for how the App handles data.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Updates and support</h2>
        <p>
          We fix what we advertise. Contact us with your Google Play order number (it starts with GPA), the
          purchase date and steps to reproduce the problem. We aim to reply within 5 business days and to fix
          it or provide a workaround within 14 business days. Refund timing is in our{' '}
          <a href="/refund-policy/" class="text-link">refund policy</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Warranties and your statutory rights</h2>
        <p>
          We provide the App with reasonable care and skill, but we cannot promise it is error-free or that
          it will run on every device or with every file. As far as the law allows, the App is provided “as
          is” and we exclude other warranties and conditions that would otherwise apply.
        </p>
        <p>
          None of this affects your statutory rights. If you are a consumer, the Consumer Rights Act 2015
          requires digital content to be as described, fit for purpose and of satisfactory quality, and
          nothing in these terms removes or limits those rights.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Our liability</h2>
        <p>
          We do not exclude or limit our liability where it would be unlawful to do so. This includes
          liability for death or personal injury caused by our negligence, for fraud, and, if you are a
          consumer, for damage to your device or to other digital content caused by our failure to use
          reasonable care and skill.
        </p>
        <p>
          Subject to that, we are not liable for loss that was not reasonably foreseeable, for loss of data
          you could have backed up, or for indirect or consequential loss. Our total liability in
          connection with the App is limited to the amount you paid for it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Termination</h2>
        <p>
          You can stop using the App at any time by uninstalling it. We may end your licence only if you
          materially breach these terms; we will not arbitrarily withdraw a licence you have paid for. If
          your licence ends, you must stop using the App. Any refund right you have already earned, and your
          statutory rights, are not affected.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>
          We version this page. See the Last updated date and time above. If we make a material change, we
          add a dated note here and announce it on our blog at least 7 days before it takes effect. A change
          will not reduce what your purchase covers. Continuing to use the App after a change takes effect
          means you accept the updated terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are governed by the law of England and Wales, and disputes are subject to the courts of
          England and Wales. If you are a consumer living in Scotland or Northern Ireland, you can also bring
          proceedings in your local courts, and you keep the benefit of any mandatory consumer protections
          that apply where you live.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these terms use our{' '}
          <a href="/contact/" class="text-link">contact form</a> or email us at{' '}
          <button type="button" data-mailto={site.mail} class="text-link">{site.emailDisplay}</button>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
